Session 14 summary — criteria **not yet met** (marker not written), but this was the biggest convergence session of the run: first-ever full-suite passes at every node count, and the last remaining correctness bug is now captured to the millisecond.

**Landed and verified this session (final build `4D677327`):**

1. **SF-dir tenure floor** (`mxfs_dlm_sf_tenure_keep_delay/arm` + both eager unhold gates): the root of tds-8-node's 72s was 2.4 dir-EX handoffs per round — every syscall boundary handed the lock away because MHT never covered shell exec gaps. The floor keeps a young shortform-dir EX across idle gaps with the dwork serving the peer at expiry. tds standalone: 72s → 41.7s PASS 8/8.
2. **`dir_sf_mht_ms` 15→40**: in-suite, per-op time inflates ~2× (aged log across 17 tests on one mount), so 15ms tenures stopped batching. At 40ms: **iter r8 = 17/17 — the first full-suite 8/tcp pass ever — reproduced by r9 on the compiled default**, tds 17-31s with 2× margin, cache_coherency clean.
3. **FIX-F** (miss-reload li_list gate): proved the ds got=0 loop was the P91 guard re-serving a stale in-core cluster image after every invalidate (invalidate only checked the bli, not foreign slots' log items) — FIX-E's slot patch was gated behind the wrong condition and never ran. dlm_scaling passed every iter since.
4. **FIX-G** (destage-then-reload, gap≥3): the 2/tcp shutdown root was P34F treating a *stuck-flush* dirty ili as authority while peers advanced the dir 13 generations, then RMW-ing the stale base into `xfs_dir2_data_use_free` corruption. First version destage-stormed the hot path (2/tcp tds crippled); the gap≥3 gate fixed it — 2/tcp 17/17 on the final build.
5. **Harness/infra**: suite_iter 8-node timeout 1100→2600 (was silently truncating iters), drc stale-`/root` forensics cleanup (stale files from prior boots poisoned two post-mortems), bounded drop_caches with kernel-stack capture (two silent node-death iters traced to an eviction interlock in the test's cold-cache step), P14 iflush/rebase tripwires against publishing desynced SF images.

**Column status:** 8/tcp 17/17 ×2 then 15/17 (r10); 4/tcp 17/17; 2/tcp 17/17 ×2 of 4; 1/tcp 16/16.

**The one remaining correctness bug**, captured exactly in r10 round 4: node4's dirent add committed and published **3-9ms into node6's EX tenure** (N6 FUA-read a 73-entry base at +3.6546, N4's 74-entry write submitted +3.6579, N6's divergent 74-entry write at +3.6647 won the block) — a mutual-exclusion break at the tenure boundary, most likely an admitted-but-not-yet-pinned op window slipping past the release's quiescence check. Full forensics, fix candidates, and instrumentation plan are in ccmemory (`sess14run-DECISIVE-one-dirent-swallow-is-tenure-boundary-mutex-race`). Next session: instrument the phantom-EX writer, close the admit/release race, then accumulate repeated clean iters on all four columns before writing the marker.

